      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not draining them; in many ways, your presence may help guide memories and provide the support they need to navigate their own grief. The \"math\" you are describing is a cruel illusion created by survival guilt, which tells you that if you were gone too, it would somehow make things easier for them, but life continues without a logical equation. Please consider speaking with a therapist who specializes in trauma and survivor guilt to help untangle these painful thoughts from the reality of your love for them.",
